## Pros and Cons of a Marquise Diamond Eternity Band

**Pros**

- Most dramatic visual profile of any eternity band style
- Elongated stones maximize the appearance of band width on the finger
- Lab-grown certified bands start at [$1,895](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/eternity-ring-with-2-ctw-marquise-cut-lab-grown-diamonds-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-297275?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — 60–75% less than natural at the same certified grade
- East-west orientation design eliminates the most common prong failure mechanism

**Cons**

- V-tip prongs require 6-month inspection intervals, versus 12 months for round-prong bands
- Retipping costs 3× more than round-prong eternity bands due to stone removal
- Full eternity bands cannot be resized at any point after purchase
- Requires a skilled setter — incorrect V-prong orientation accelerates all five failure types above

