## Care and Cleaning for a Marquise Diamond Eternity Band

The V-tip prongs are also the first spots where dirt and residue accumulate. Lotion, soap film, and skin oils collect in the V-channel between the prong and stone surface. This buildup is invisible to the eye but creates a micro-abrasive paste under the prong — accelerating the same tip-wear described in Issue 1.

Clean your band every two weeks at home. Use warm water, a few drops of dish soap, and a soft toothbrush. Focus the brush directly on each V-prong tip. Rinse under warm running water and dry with a lint-free cloth.

Avoid ultrasonic cleaners for marquise eternity bands. The ultrasonic vibration transmits directly through the prong-and-stone structure. For a band with any prong drift or looseness — conditions that may not be visible yet — ultrasonic vibration can dislodge a stone. Get a professional ultrasonic clean only after a jeweler has confirmed all prongs are tight.

Remove the band before gym use, gardening, or any activity involving gripping under load. These are the highest-torque activities and the fastest source of prong drift. A [marquise pave engagement ring](/marquise-pave-engagement-ring) or bezel-set alternative is worth considering if removal isn't practical.

