**If you want the best structural design for stacking:** The [east-west marquise eternity ring at $3,250](https://www.bluenile.com/wedding-rings/east-west-eternity-ring-with-marquise-cut-diamonds-in-14k-white-gold-200mm-by-james-allen-item-305001?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the only option that solves the tip-to-tip prong contact problem by design. It pairs cleanly with a classic marquise solitaire without prong-on-prong interference.

**If you want maximum visual impact:** The [3ctw white gold at $2,750](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/eternity-ring-with-3-ctw-marquise-cut-lab-grown-diamonds-in-14k-white-gold-item-297276?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) delivers the most sparkle at a certified lab price. Go in knowing you're committing to the 6-month inspection schedule — not the standard 12-month.

**If you wear your ring during physical activity:** Choose a half-eternity design. The solid underside absorbs flex forces that a full eternity band transfers directly to the prongs. Your long-term maintenance cost drops by 40–50%.

