## Expert Summary

Farzana Hasan, diamond expert at DiamondCritics, has evaluated marquise diamond eternity bands for 15+ years of professional setting and advisory work. Full credentials at [/about-farzana/](/about-farzana/).

The marquise diamond eternity band delivers a level of visual drama no other eternity band matches. The elongated stone silhouette and continuous V-tip sparkle are unlike anything in round or oval band formats. But it is the most maintenance-demanding band style available — and that demand is predictable if you know where to look.

The five prong failure patterns in this guide are all preventable. You need three things: a setter who understands the Alternating V-Tip Principle, a commitment to 6-month inspection intervals, and a jeweler who retips V-prongs in-house. Follow those three rules and your marquise diamond eternity band looks as good at year 15 as it does today. Ignore them, and you're looking at a significant repair bill before year 5.

For stone selection before choosing your band, see the [lab-grown marquise diamond guide](/lab-grown-marquise-diamond) or the pillar [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond). For [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/) grading standards on marquise stones, visit gia.edu. For [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) certificate verification on any lab-grown stone, visit igi.org.
